@startuml
title L1 components: entry points, host authority and model access
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
top to bottom direction
component "React browser client\nEnglish / Persian + RTL\nplain-text replies, session cookie and CSRF" as browser #F6EBDC
rectangle "Python application modules / logical boundaries" #E8F0FA {
  component "FastAPI entry point\nweb.py\nHost, Origin, JSON and locale checks" as web
  component "Terminal entry point\ncli.py\nhost-created principal and operator options" as cli
  rectangle "Code-owned authority" #EDF7ED {
    component "LangGraph workflow\nworkflow.py\ninput review -> mixing OR production -> output review\ncode validates evidence and commits accepted turns" as graph
    database "ContextStore\ncontext.py\nowner, tenant, readers, TTL and capacity" as context
    file "Startup policy\npolicy.py + policy.json\nstrict schemas, rules, thresholds and digest" as policy
  }
  component "LangChain provider adapter\nproviders.py + resilience.py\nshared specialist circuit / judge circuit / audit circuit\ndeadlines, capacity and strict model outputs" as adapter #FBE9E4
  component "Evaluation entry point\nevaluation.py + auditing.py\nsynthetic fixtures and independent expected outcomes\noptional post-run auditor; validated metadata report" as evaluation #F3EAF6
}
node "Selected model service\nloopback Ollama OR OpenAI API\nall model output remains untrusted" as provider #FBE9E4
browser --> web : HTTP / JSON
web --> graph : HOST CONTEXT
cli --> graph : HOST CONTEXT
graph --> context : OWNER CHECK
policy --> graph : ENFORCE RULES
policy --> evaluation : EVAL POLICY
graph --> adapter : THREE CALLS
evaluation ..> graph : SYNTHETIC RUN
evaluation ..> adapter : OPTIONAL AUDIT
adapter --> provider : MODEL CALL
legend bottom
Four runtime LLM roles; code controls routing, output release and memory writes.
Boxes describe code responsibilities, not separate deployed services.
Web, terminal and evaluation are alternative entry points using the same core modules.
Evaluation uses its own state and clients; the audit-fixture suite calls only the auditor.
The auditor cannot change policy, expected labels or completed chat outcomes.
Provider, policy and credentials come from the operator, never chat text.
Solid arrows: runtime calls or policy input. Dashed arrows: evaluation-only calls.
L1 expands the application from L0 (13); detailed safety boundaries are in 07 and 08.
endlegend
footer Agentic Drink Book | Policy 2.1.0 | Model judgments remain fallible
@enduml
